BT /F1 24 Tf 50 720 Td (SYNAPSE OS: MACHINE LEARNING ESSENTIALS) Tj /F1 12 Tf 0 -30 Td (Lecture Notes & Research Summary) Tj 0 -25 Td (1. NEURAL NETWORKS & BACKPROPAGATION) Tj 0 -18 Td (A neural network is a collection of connected units or nodes called artificial neurons.) Tj 0 -15 Td (Each connection transmits a signal, which is a real number computed by an activation function.) Tj 0 -25 Td (2. LOSS FUNCTIONS & GRADIENT DESCENT) Tj 0 -18 Td (Mean Squared Error (MSE): L = 1/N * sum((y_true - y_pred)^2)) Tj 0 -15 Td (Cross-Entropy Loss: L = -sum(y_true * log(y_pred))) Tj 0 -15 Td (Optimization: theta = theta - lr * grad(L)) Tj 0 -25 Td (3. REGULARIZATION TECHNIQUES) Tj 0 -18 Td (- L1 Regularization (Lasso): Promotes sparsity in weights) Tj 0 -15 Td (- L2 Regularization (Ridge / Weight Decay): Prevents extreme weights) Tj 0 -15 Td (- Dropout: Randomly zeros activations during forward pass with probability p) Tj 0 -25 Td (4. TRANSFORMER ARCHITECTURE) Tj 0 -18 Td (Self-Attention mechanism: Attention(Q, K, V) = softmax(Q * K^T / sqrt(d_k)) * V) Tj 0 -15 Td (Multi-Head Attention allows the model to jointly attend to information from different representation subspaces.) Tj ET
